{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>And Moses sent his father-in-law.</b> For he did not wish to go with Israel to the land, as it says: לֹא אֵלֵךְ כִּי אִם אֶל אַרְצִי וְאֶל מוֹלַדְתִּי אֵלֵךְ (Numbers 10:30). This was perhaps on account of his old age, like the case of Barzillai, who said: יָשׁוּב נָא עַבְדְּךָ וָאָמֹת בְּעִירִי, עִם קֶבֶר אָבִי וְאִמִּי (2 Samuel 19:38). But the children of Jethro went with Israel to the land without doubt, as it says: וּבְנֵי קֵינִי חֹתֵן מֹשֶׁה עָלוּ מֵעִיר הַתְּמָרִים וגו׳ (Judges 1:16), and concerning them Balaam said: אֵיתָן מוֹשָׁבְךָ כוּ׳ (Numbers 24:21)."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:26:13.139513899Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}